  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Native Material3 task UI",
    "overview": "Native Material3 task UI: familiar controls, readable terms, quiet feedback. System typography and dynamic color make Settings feel at home on Android; the green palette is the static fallback.\n\nThis records the implemented Settings/dictionary surface, not a redesign of the recording UI. No imagery or custom display face is needed for this task.\n\nVerification: on-phone `DictionarySettingsTest` passed default dark and app-local light previews; light explicitly used fontScale 1.3 without changing device settings. Assertions covered visible IME, commit above IME, action targets of at least 48dp, duplicate/search/valid/empty states. Actual successful UI Add/repeat behavior is code-reviewed, not automated through a successful UI save; backend persistence/update is tested separately.\n\nFinal contrast correction (`c23d2f1`): search hint explicitly uses `colorOnSurfaceVariant`; measured hint contrast is 4.94:1 in light and 6.56:1 in dark. Four list/empty contrast recaptures under `corpus/lab/dictionary-settings-contrast-review/files/lab/dictionary-settings/` (`phone-list.png`, `phone-empty.png`, `phone-large-light-list.png`, `phone-large-light-empty.png`) supersede the corresponding earlier captures for contrast only. Add/duplicate evidence remains in the final-review directory. Both dark and app-local light/1.3-scale UI tests passed again on the final APK, including keyboard and touch-target checks.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Native Android Material3 controls.",
      "Dynamic color with light/dark green fallbacks.",
      "One-field editing and immediate per-entry saving."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "System Color",
        "body": "Resolve semantic theme attributes at runtime; static green values are fallbacks, not a forced brand palette.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Native Type",
        "body": "Use Android text appearances and scalable sp text; preserve the system font.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "Native Depth",
        "body": "Let Material widgets own elevation, state layers and transitions; do not introduce a separate shadow system.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use semantic theme colors and DayNight resources.",
      "**Do** preserve at least 48dp action targets, system insets and keyboard accommodation.",
      "**Do** keep saving feedback close to the field and provide Undo after deletion.",
      "**Do** keep dictionary management in Settings and recording focused on recording."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** hardcode the fallback green over dynamic color.",
      "**Don't** add a global Save step to the per-entry editor.",
      "**Don't** promise measured accuracy gains for arbitrary new terms."
    ]
  }
